---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import InterestForm from "../components/InterestForm.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Moving to Andorra from the UK | Official pathways"
  description="What a UK move to Andorra actually involves: Andorran immigration on Govern.ad, passport documents, banks and housing. Hedged. No invented tax rates."
  path="/moving-to-andorra-from-the-uk"
>
  <section class="page-header">
    <h1>Moving from the United Kingdom</h1>
    <p>
      Andorra is not in the United Kingdom, the EU or the EEA. A British move
      is an Andorran immigration file. UK tax residence is a separate question
      for UK advisers.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <div class="notice">
      <p>
        Official letter codes and BOPA amounts are on
        <a href="/become-a-resident">become a resident</a>.
        An English practitioner map — Jane Whittaker’s
        <a
          href="https://www.livinginandorra.com/residency_options.html"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener">Living in Andorra 2026 page</a
        >
        — uses a different A/B/C/D alphabet. Her A is not official A.1.
        The whole-site reading is on
        <a href="/practitioner-map">the practitioner map</a>.
        Use
        <a
          href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/tematiques/immigracio/residencia-i-treball"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener">Govern.ad</a
        >
        and counsel in both countries.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>Immigration is Andorran</h2>
    <p>
      The Servei d’Immigració publishes the same families of authorisation for
      everyone: residence and work (including A.1 for an employer and
      self-employed J.1 — Compte Propi in English rooms) and residence without
      work (D.1). In Jane Whittaker’s map, D.1 without lucrative activity is
      “Category A”, D.1.2 is “B”, D.1.3 is “C”, and J.1 is “D”. Official B.1
      is family reunification, not her B. A digital-nomad route (D.3) is still
      on the official residence index; she states that she does not process
      D.3 or entrepreneur files. Start with
      <a href="/become-a-resident">become a resident</a>
      and the live Government pages.
    </p>
    <p>
      On the current
      <a
        href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/tematiques/immigracio/residencia-i-treball/residencia-i-treball-autoritzacio-inicial"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">A.1 page</a
      >, nationals of EU and EEA states may present a national identity card
      instead of a passport. The United Kingdom is not listed there as an EU or
      EEA state. In practice that means a British applicant should expect to
      present a valid passport, plus the rest of the published file — criminal
      records, accommodation, civil status, and whatever the chosen route
      requires. Confirm this on the page that matches your route, not from this
      summary.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Government also publishes a note on residence-and-work authorisations
      for extra-community nationals. Whether that note applies to your file is
      a question for immigration and for counsel — we do not decide it here.
    </p>

    <h2>Conventions</h2>
    <p>
      The Ministry of Justice and Interior lists a 2001 convention with Spain
      and France, and a 2007 convention with Portugal, on entry, circulation
      and establishment. We do not treat the United Kingdom as a party to those
      texts. Renewal cycles on official pages sometimes differ for “nationals
      of states that have signed and ratified a convention”. That is another
      reason to read the live A.1 / D.1 / D.3 page rather than a UK blog.
    </p>

    <h2>Tax is not the permit</h2>
    <p>
      An Andorran immigration authorisation is not, by itself, UK tax
      non-residence, and it is not Andorran tax residence. Several D.1 pages
      speak of 90 days; article 8 of Law 5/2014 uses 183 days or the centre
      of interests —
      <a href="/tax-residence">tax residence</a>.
      The
      <a
        href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/tematiques/impostos-taxes-i-duana"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">Ministeri de Finances</a
      >
      publishes Andorran tax rules. Leaving the UK for tax purposes is a UK
      question. Do not rely on a rate you have heard socially.
    </p>

    <h2>Banks, housing, schools</h2>
    <p>
      Opening an Andorran account is a KYC meeting, not an online form. See
      <a href="/opening-a-bank-account">opening a bank account</a>.
      Buying before you are resident usually needs a foreign-investment
      authorisation:
      <a href="/buying-property">buying property</a>.
      Education and healthcare are on
      <a href="/education">education</a>
      and
      <a href="/healthcare">healthcare</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Counsel and gestories with official sites are in the
      <a href="/directory">directory</a>,
      including
      <a href="/directory/jane-whittaker">Jane Whittaker / J W Serveis</a>.
      The wider move note is
      <a href="/moving-to-andorra">moving to Andorra</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <InterestForm
    intro="Leave your details if you are considering a move from the UK."
    source="moving-from-uk"
  />
</Base>
